  "response": "Read all four call sites plus `button.tsx` to check what actually varies. Here's the proposal.\n\n## The finding\n\n`crime_00071` — **Duplicate Component Shape**, medium / confidence 0.70, hash `e96b55b64336`, 4 files × 4 occurrences:\n\n| File | Lines |\n|---|---|\n| `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx` | 142–150 |\n| `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx` | 152–160 |\n| `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx` | 101–109 |\n| `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx` | 112–120 |\n\nThe subtree is the **form action footer** — the last child of `<form>`, after the `bg-gray-50` field panel:\n\n```tsx\n<div className=\"mt-6 flex justify-end gap-4\">\n  <Link\n    href=\"/dashboard/invoices\"\n    className=\"flex h-10 items-center rounded-lg bg-gray-100 px-4 text-sm font-medium text-gray-600 transition-colors hover:bg-gray-200\"\n  >\n    Cancel\n  </Link>\n  <Button type=\"submit\">Create Invoice</Button>\n</div>\n```\n\nA repo-wide grep for `mt-6 flex justify-end gap-4` returns exactly these four and nothing else — the detector's occurrence set is complete, so the refactor has no stragglers.\n\n**What varies:** only the submit label — `\"Create Invoice\"` vs `\"Edit Invoice\"`. The wrapper classes, the `Link` href, the `Link`'s 11-utility class string, and the `Cancel` text are byte-identical in all four. That's the drift risk: the cancel button is styled as a hand-rolled ghost button that duplicates `Button`'s `h-10 rounded-lg px-4 text-sm font-medium` geometry with no shared source. Change the button height or radius in `app/ui/button.tsx` and these four cancel links silently stop matching.\n\n## Scope caveat, stated up front\n\n`final-example` and `starter-example` are two independent Next.js apps with separate `package.json` and separate `@/` aliases. **One component cannot span them** without introducing a shared workspace package, which is well beyond this fixture's shape. So this is two parallel extractions, 2 call sites each — 4 hand-maintained copies become 2 definitions. If you do want a single definition, that's a different (larger) change: a `packages/ui` workspace both apps depend on.\n\n## Files that would change\n\n**New (2):**\n- `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/form-actions.tsx`\n- `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/form-actions.tsx`\n\n**Edited (4)** — each drops its 9-line footer, adds one import, renders one element:\n- `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx` (−9 / +1 at L142)\n- `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx` (−9 / +1 at L152)\n- `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx` (−9 / +1 at L101)\n- `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx` (−9 / +1 at L112)\n\n`Link` and `Button` imports become unused in all four files if the footer was their only consumer — it is, in all four. Drop them.\n\n## Public API\n\n```tsx\nimport Link from 'next/link';\nimport { Button } from '@/app/ui/button';\n\nexport interface FormActionsProps {\n  /** Route the Cancel link returns to. */\n  cancelHref: string;\n  /** Submit button text — the only thing that differs between create and edit. */\n  submitLabel: string;\n  /** Cancel link text. */\n  cancelLabel?: string;          // default: 'Cancel'\n  /** Marks submit as aria-disabled; Button already styles this state. */\n  pending?: boolean;             // default: false\n  /** Slot: extra actions rendered left of Cancel (e.g. Delete on edit). */\n  children?: React.ReactNode;\n}\n\nexport function FormActions({\n  cancelHref,\n  submitLabel,\n  cancelLabel = 'Cancel',\n  pending = false,\n  children,\n}: FormActionsProps) {\n  return (\n    <div className=\"mt-6 flex justify-end gap-4\">\n      {children}\n      <Link\n        href={cancelHref}\n        className=\"flex h-10 items-center rounded-lg bg-gray-100 px-4 text-sm font-medium text-gray-600 transition-colors hover:bg-gray-200\"\n      >\n        {cancelLabel}\n      </Link>\n      <Button type=\"submit\" aria-disabled={pending}>\n        {submitLabel}\n      </Button>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n**Slots:** one — `children`, positioned *before* Cancel so the destructive/secondary action sits farthest from submit. That's the only extension point the current call sites need; edit-form is the obvious future consumer (a Delete action).\n\n**Props defended:**\n- `cancelHref` is **required**, not defaulted to `/dashboard/invoices`, even though all four pass that exact value. A default would make the component quietly invoice-specific and would be wrong the moment a customers form reuses it — which is the point of extracting it.\n- `pending` exists because `Button`'s className already carries `aria-disabled:cursor-not-allowed aria-disabled:opacity-50` styling that nothing currently triggers. Both forms already hold `useActionState` state; wiring pending through is a one-line follow-up per call site, not part of this refactor.\n\n**Deliberately not props:**\n- `className` on the wrapper — an override prop reopens exactly the drift this closes. If a caller needs different layout, that's a second component.\n- Submit `variant`/`color` — belongs to `Button`, not here.\n- The cancel link's class string — should eventually become a `Button` variant (`<Button as={Link} variant=\"secondary\">`), which is the real fix for the geometry duplication. Out of scope here; flagging it as the next step.\n\n## Call sites after\n\n```tsx\n// create-form.tsx\n<FormActions cancelHref=\"/dashboard/invoices\" submitLabel=\"Create Invoice\" />\n\n// edit-form.tsx\n<FormActions cancelHref=\"/dashboard/invoices\" submitLabel=\"Edit Invoice\" />\n```\n\n## Risk and verification\n\n`blast_radius` is 0 (no importers), `test_gap` 0.5 (no tests) — nothing depends on these files, so the failure mode is purely visual. Verify by rendering `/dashboard/invoices/create` and `/dashboard/invoices/[id]/edit` in each app and confirming the footer is pixel-identical; the extracted JSX is a literal move, so any diff means a typo in the class strings.\n\n## What this does *not* fix\n\nTwo adjacent findings in the same files stay open and want separate changes:\n- `crime_00072` / `crime_00073` — `invoice.status === 'paid'` / `'pending'` duplicated across edit-form and status.tsx in both apps. That's a policy helper, not a component.\n- `crime_00074` / `crime_00075` / `crime_00078` / `crime_00079` — `design_token_escape`, the `h-[18px] w-[18px]` and `px-[14px]` arbitrary values in the field panel. Those live above the footer and are untouched by this extraction.",
